    Bug 1923421 - Fix missing onMoved and onCopied event for some cross-server operations. r=mkmelin

    IMAP operations are somewhat special. The 4th `dstMsgs` parameter of
    the `MailServices.mfn.msgsMoveCopyCompleted` event can be empty,
    because the messages have not yet been fully added to the destination.
    Up until now we skipped such events and did not report them.

    We do however know the folder where the messages *should* appear in.
    This patch is forcing the server to update the destination folder and is
    using the `MailServices.mfn.msgAdded` event to monitor the destination
    folder for newly added messages. The `messages.onMoved` and `onCopied`
    events are delayed until all expeced destination messages have been
    seen. The `headerMessageId` is used to match source and destination
    messages.

    We also have to deal with a speciality of some IMAP move operations
    (reproducible with local-to-IMAP-moves), which report invalid src
    msgHdrs, because the message is already removed when the
    `msgsMoveCopyCompleted` event is fired. This is solved by introducing a
    temporary cache which is populated through the
    `Ci.nsIFolderListener.onMessageRemoved` event.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D224970

